== Ownership and safety review
<ownership-and-safety-review>
Use one accountable owner per control. Required co-approvers for
high-consequence changes are the district incident command, qualified
fire/AHJ reviewer where applicable, accessibility lead, privacy counsel,
independent evaluator and, for police operations, the authorized
law-enforcement agency. Community participation and an independent
complaint channel are mandatory for legitimacy.

== Qualification gates
<qualification-gates>
+ #strong[Necessity:] why this threat is materially relevant and
  baseline safeguards insufficient.
+ #strong[Safety:] no egress trapping, unacceptable false alarms, added
  injury, or unmeasured cascading behavior.
+ #strong[Rights:] documented legal basis, no ownership registry, no
  ideological targeting or coercion, records purpose restrictions.
+ #strong[Cyber:] verified vendor update chain, segmentation and safe
  manual recovery.
+ #strong[Independent evidence:] test logs reproducible and decision
  signed by parties not financially dependent on selected vendor.

#callout(warning: true)[
#strong[Mandatory STOP:] unqualified armed activity, a proposed
automatic use-of-force feature, unapproved student surveillance, an
egress-related critical defect, unlawful sharing of education records,
or any request to publish exploitable site details.
]
== Metrics dashboard
<metrics-dashboard>
Report validated risk-reduction proxies: opt-in uptake and
comprehension; false-report escalation and correction; alert reach and
latency distributions; successful accessible evacuation/egress checks;
kit and skills readiness; cyber restoration outcomes; completed case
reviews; community complaints and their resolution. Do not infer
casualty reduction from pilot proxies alone.

== Deliverable at day 90
<deliverable-at-day-90>
An independent acceptance memo records for each scenario:
#strong[approve low-risk measure / fund corrective action / limit to
offline pilot / suspend or reject]. Maintain a future review cadence
driven by emerging threat evidence and control failures, not a calendar
purchase quota.
